So the parsed attribute value is correct: `data:image/png;base64,AAAA` (no space). The first case (alone) works. The second case produces `data:image/png;base64, AAAA`. So the issue is in my segmentation when the data URL candidate is NOT first... 

Trace: value = "a.jpg 1x, custom:thing 2x, data:image/png;base64,AAAA".

- pos=0: scan "a.jpg" → space → inUrl=false → "1x" → ',' at index 8 → not inUrl → break. Segment "a.jpg 1x" ✓. pos=9.
- pos=9: " custom:thing 2x, data..." — space → inUrl=false; "custom:thing" → space; "2x" → ',' → not inUrl → break. Segment " custom:thing 2x" ✓. pos = index of that comma + 1.
- Now pos points at " data:image/png;base64,AAAA". scan: ' ' → inUrl=false!! Then "data:image/png;base64" → comma → inUrl is FALSE → break! Segment = " data:image/png;base64" → candidate "data:image/png;base64". Then next segment "AAAA".

The bug: `inUrl` is set to false by the LEADING whitespace of the candidate (before the address). The leading whitespace gets trimmed later, but it already flipped inUrl. Fix: inUrl should only become false after the address has started — i.e., whitespace before any non-whitespace content shouldn't count. Better: track whether we've seen the first non-whitespace char. Whitespace only ends the URL scan if we've already consumed non-whitespace (address) chars.

Fix: `if (isSrcsetSpace(c)) { if (seenContent) inUrl = false; } else { seenContent = true; ... }` — actually simpler: `inUrl = inUrl && !isSrcsetSpace(c)` is wrong for leading ws. Use: only set inUrl=false if some non-whitespace was seen in this candidate. Let me restructure:

```java
boolean inUrl = true; // still scanning the URL run (no whitespace after URL content yet)
boolean started = false; // seen non-whitespace in this candidate
while (end < length) {
    char c = value.charAt(end);
