        if (inUrl && started && end + 1 < length && !isSrcsetSpace(value.charAt(end + 1)) && value.charAt(end + 1) != ',')
            end++;
        else
            break;
    } else {
        if (isSrcsetSpace(c)) {
            if (started) inUrl = false;
        } else {
            started = true;
        }
        end++;
    }
}
```

Note: `started` implies end > start for the comma case, so I can drop `end > start` and use `started`. Wait — comma at candidate start: started=false → break → separator ✓. Comma after leading whitespace " ,a": started=false → separator ✓ (empty candidate). Comma right after address chars: started=true, inUrl=true → check next ✓.

Hmm wait, but there's a subtlety: "a ,b" — 'a' → started; ' ' → inUrl=false; ',' → not inUrl → separator ✓.

Also: what about a comma encountered when started=true but inUrl already false → separator ✓.

Edge: leading whitespace then comma then non-ws: " ,a" → comma: started=false → separator → segment " " → empty → dropped; then "a" ✓.

Let me apply this fix.

